941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)"}},{"titleInfo":{"title":"Karl Polanyi","subTitle":"the limits of the market"},"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Dale, Gareth.","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Cambridge. Eng"}},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Malden, MA"}}],"publisher":"Polity","dateIssued":["c2010",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2010"}],"issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"viii, 309 p. ; 23 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Karl Polanyi's The Great Transformation is generally acclaimed as being among the most influential works of economic history in the twentieth century, and remains as vital in the current historical conjuncture as it was in his own. In its critique of nineteenth-century \"market fundamentalism\" it reads as a warning to our own neoliberal age, and is widely touted as a prophetic guidebook for those who aspire to understand the causes and dynamics of global economic turbulence at the end of the 2000s. Karl Polanyi: The Limits of the Market is the first comprehensive introduction to Polanyi's ideas and legacy. It assesses not only the texts for which he is famous -- prepared during his spells in American academia -- but also his journalistic articles written in his first exile in Vienna, and lectures and pamphlets from his second exile, in Britain. It provides a detailed critical analysis of The Great Transformation, but also surveys Polanyi's seminal writings in economic anthropology, the economic history of ancient and archaic societies, and political and economic theory. Its primary source base includes interviews with Polanyi's daughter, Kari Polanyi-Levitt, as well as the entire compass of his own published and unpublished writings in English and German. This engaging and accessible introduction to Polanyi's thinking will appeal to students and scholars across the social sciences, providing a refreshing perspective on the roots of our current economic crisis. -- Back cover."},"tableOfContents":"Introduction -- 1. The economics and ethics of socialism -- 2. The great transformation -- 3. The descent of economic man -- 4. Trade, markets and money in archaic societies -- 5. \"Disembedded\" and \"always embedded\" economies -- 6. At the brink of a \"great transformation\"? Neoliberalism and the countermovement today -- Conclusion.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Gareth Dale."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Polanyi, Karl",{"@type":"date","#text":"1886-1964"}]}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Polanyi, Karl",{"@type":"date","#text":"1886-1964"}]},"titleInfo":{"title":"Great transformation"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Economics","Philosophy"]}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HB102.P64 D35 2010"},{"@edition":"22","@authority":"ddc","#text":"330.1"}],"relatedItem":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Key contemporary thinkers series"}},{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"Karl Polanyi"},"name":{"namePart":"Dale, Gareth."},"originInfo":{"publisher":"Cambridge ; Malden, MA. : Polity Press, ©2010"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)761302599"}},{"@type":"series","titleInfo":{"title":"Key contemporary thinkers (Cambridge, England)"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990123560000203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780745640716 (hbk.)"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0745640710 (hbk.)"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0745640729 (pbk.)"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780745640723 (pbk.)"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"501399831"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000463633307","#text":"Lamont Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HB102.P64 D35 2010"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HB102.P64 D35 2010x"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":["Lamont","Widener"]},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990123560000203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"012356000"}},"processingDate":"2024-03-19T05:18Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"UKM"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"100106"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20100728"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990123560000203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)"}},{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":[{"@altRepGroup":"02","title":"Wang Shaoguang du Bolanni ","subTitle":"\"Da zhuan xing\" yu Zhongguo de da zhuan xing "},{"@altRepGroup":"02","title":"王紹光讀波蘭尼 ","subTitle":"《大轉型》與中國的大轉型 "},{"@type":"alternative","@altRepGroup":"03","title":"\"Da zhuan xing\" yu Zhongguo de da zhuan xing"},{"@type":"alternative","@altRepGroup":"03","title":"《大轉型》與中國的大轉型"},{"@type":"alte