roduction: The paradoxes of Karl Polanyi -- The origins of the self-regulating market -- The dynamics of a market society -- The politics of social protection -- Contradictions and crisis in the double movement -- The double movement in the contemporary era -- Transcending the double movement.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"John Vail."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."},{"@type":"reproduction","#text":"Electronic reproduction. London Available via World Wide Web."},{"@type":"biographical/historical","#text":"John Vail is currently a Visiting Professor in the School of Geography, Politics and Sociology at Newcastle University where he was previously a Senior Lecturer of Sociology until his retirement. His research interests are in egalitarian political economy. He has edited volumes on insecurity and alternative approaches to full employment and has written several articles on decommodification and egalitarian political economy. With Professor Robert Hollands, he has written a series of papers on the transformative cultural activism of the Newcastle based film and photography collective, Amber Films."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"e-uk---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Polanyi, Karl",{"@type":"date","#text":"1886-1964"}]},"titleInfo":{"title":"Great transformation"}},{"@authority":"fast","titleInfo":{"title":"Great transformation (Polanyi, Karl)"}},{"@authority":"fast","temporal":"1800-1899"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Free enterprise","Social aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Capitalism","Social aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Industries","Self-regulation"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Public welfare"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Autorégulation"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Aide sociale"},{"@authority":"aat","topic":"welfare services"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SOCIAL SCIENCE / Sociology / Gene